  "query_preview": "..Beautiful Sunday with wrap around generally flat \ncumulus across Cochise county. Water vapor imagery showed closed\nupper low over central Chihuahua MX, which will slowly push east\nover the next 24 hours. Moderate pressure gradient producing\ngusty easterly winds which will die down after sunset. \n\nMonday: Northeast flow aloft between high pressure across\nnorthern Arizona and trofiness across northern Mexico. The\ncumulus field across Cochise county should be less than today.\n\nTuesday through Thursday: High pressure aloft will provide clear\nto mostly clear conditions, terrain driven winds and daily high\ntemperatures 2-5 degrees above normal. During this time period\na Pacific weather system will move toward the west coast with\nthe southern part breaking away late on Thursday. \n\nFriday through Sunday: Southern stream system will bring\nincreased precipitation chances (30%-40% Sat/Sun). This far out\nwe have uncertainty on track, how much moisture will be advected\nnorth into the Arizona and how much precipitation will fall with\nlarge spreads in rainfall totals. High temperatures will be \ncooler, below normal, next weekend.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (Mon Nov 16 to Sun Nov 22)\nTemperature: Near normal\nPrecipitation: Likely above normal (50%-56% chance)",
